Upstream: https://gitlab-master.nvidia.com/dler/vllm/-/merge_requests/1
Author: Thinh Le (dler); backported here onto vLLM 0.29.1rc1.dev187.
Runtime change only; upstream tests omitted (matching the PR-57505 patch).

`<video>` is deliberately absent from this checkpoint's vocabulary, so it
tokenizes as three ordinary tokens ['<', 'video', '>']. When the chat template
places it directly after text, BPE merges the preceding character with '<'
(e.g. '.<'), the PromptReplacement target no longer matches, and
_validate_mm_placeholders raises:

  "Expected there to be 1 prompt placeholders corresponding to 1 video items,
   but instead found 0 prompt placeholders!"

Normalising the prompt so `<video>` always follows whitespace restores the
match. Validated by the author on SS 2.0.12 / vLLM 0.27.1: text-first and
video-first, stream and non-stream, all returned 200 (nvbug 6715494).

DEVIATION FROM UPSTREAM !1: on vLLM 0.27.1 ProcessorInputs.prompt accepts a
str, and !1 assigns the normalized string directly. On vLLM 0.29.x the field is
typed list[int], so that assignment yields HTTP 400 "must be str, not int" at
request time. This backport keeps the str path and adds a token-id path that
re-encodes after normalising. Verified by applying both container patches to a
live 0.29.1rc1.dev187 image.

Fixes the Dynamo-side occurrence tracked in nvbug 6820634.

